39488ea23e66c against a computed 2553b915563b73cc. That mismatch was BORN WITH THE ROW upstream and was RE-VERIFIED THIS RUN against the upstream git blob at HEAD ca4f83b (stored 88839488ea23e66c vs computed 2553b915563b73cc), so it is not a post-hoc payload edit and not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 50/50 rows accounted for, of which 47 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from an upstream authoring slip; NOT 'chain-intact'. ORPHAN ROWS: 14 bot_started rows have no immediately-following witness_note (rows 1, 3, 5, 7, 10, 13, 15, 17, 18, 19, 23, 28, 35, and row 50 = this run's own, which this note closes) -- the signature of polls launched and dying before their note was written, not evidence of canon transitions. Event census over the 50 rows: 27 bot_started, 13 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll. Environment (19th consecutive wipe with the named path gone): /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, and a git clone straight into it would die with 'close error: Disk quota exceeded' on .git/description. Recovery this run: a blobless clone (--filter=blob:none --sparse) of SuperInstance/AI-Writings to the overlay at /tmp, then staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to the upstream git blob at HEAD ca4f83b and to the value recorded in every prior run; no code changes were needed this run. NEW OBSERVATION THIS RUN -- the overlay reclaimed the clone directory mid-session (/tmp/aw was gone by 20:18Z, deleted by the host rather than by this run); the staged /tmp/wm-run tree and the durable git copy were unaffected, and a second blobless clone (aw2) was re-fetched to continue verification. SUBSTRATE TRUNCATION TRAP, re-verified live this run rather than assumed: a 'cp' of substrate-witness.jsonl and topics.json to the NAS returned 'failed to close ... Disk quota exceeded' and landed as 0-byte stubs that still appeared in ls -la with nonzero-looking names; fixed without touching the script by symlinking the two NAS target files to their /tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus/ counterparts, with read-through confirming 660 and 4508 bytes. This run appended no substrate event, which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll leaves substrate-witness.jsonl byte-unchanged (md5 1a9289b50aef536c4736816ad32bc3dc, 660 bytes). CARRIED FORWARD, still PROVEN rather than merely reported: the bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0 defect. The predicate abs(gamma+eta-budget) < 1e-6 or (delta_gamma==0 and delta_eta==0) has an UNREACHABLE (0,0) escape clause on every call path (first_poll always passes delta_gamma=1.0; canon_changed always passes delta_eta=1.0), and the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Thirteenth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob, so no patch was applied.", "canon_poll": "OK 200 -- no change vs 2026-10-22T20:04Z baseline (stable ~24.2h)", "baseline_hash": "b20375d389cb505d", "canon_count": 71, "canon_changed": false, "verified_by": "watcher poll_canon() + independent curl probe before AND after the run (HTTP 200, 13720 bytes, sha256(json, sort_keys)[:16] match)", "script_md5": "206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267", "upstream_clone_head": "ca4f83b", "witness_rows": 50, "inherited_row_audit": "47/47 machine rows verify; 2 RECOVERED markers; 1 stale hash (row 25) re-verified upstream-born against git blob at HEAD ca4f83b", "orphan_rows": 14, "orphan_detail": "14 bot_started rows with no immediately-following witness_note (rows 1,3,5,7,10,13,15,17,18,19,23,28,35 plus this run's row 50, closed by this note)", "event_census": "50 rows: 27 bot_started, 13 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll", "workspace_status": "NAS mount 100% full, 0 bytes avail; /workspace/repos absent; recovered via blobless clone to overlay /tmp then staged to /tmp/wm-run (19th wipe)", "open_defect": "bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0; (0,0) escape clause proven UNREACHABLE on all call paths, so last_conserved is False everywhere and carries no signal"}, "hash": "14824bad1ed01108"}
